# Landry database (LANDRY_DATABASE_DESIGN.md) -- derived, rebuildable from
# the workbook via `python -m landry.migrate_to_db`. landry/models.py and
# landry/migrate_to_db.py ARE tracked.
landry.db
landry.db-wal
landry.db-shm

# Web UI auth (secrets — never commit)
webapp_users.json
webapp_secret.key

# Regenerated on every run (landry refresh / landry daily) -- safe to lose
landry_snapshot.json
landry_actions.json

# landry_scores.json is NOT in either category above: no credentials in
# it, and nothing regenerates a lost approval history -- it's the actual
# Part 12 audit trail (who approved what score, when, and why). It was
# gitignored by mistake alongside the two secrets above and got silently
# wiped once as a result (2026-08, GE/PH/ETN's approval history lost with
# no backup). Track it -- it keeps living as this separately-tracked,
# diffable backup even after the database lands; see design decision 2 in
# LANDRY_DATABASE_DESIGN.md.

LANDRY_SYSTEM_WORKBOOK_*_filled_*.xlsx
LANDRY_SYSTEM_WORKBOOK_*.xlsx.bak

# Alan's local viewing copy (Finder "duplicate" naming) -- lets him watch
# the live file while an edit is in progress without touching the same
# file handle; not a second source of truth, never commit it.
# Real naming convention in use is "<name>_copy.<ext>" (underscore, not the
# space Finder's own Duplicate command would produce) -- match that.
*_copy.xlsx
*_copy.docx

# Excel/Office lock files (created while a workbook is open, any OS)
~$*.xlsx
~$*.xls
~$*.docx
